---
name: setup-pre-commit
description: Set up or repair a shared gate entrypoint and local pre-commit and pre-push Git hooks for a repository. Use for installing local commit checks or unifying existing checks behind one gate. Do not use for standalone GitHub Actions workflow authoring (use setup-a-repo), PR review, or release publication.
type: agent-skill
title: Setup Pre Commit
okf_status: active
tags: [internal, operations]
---
# Setup Pre Commit

Give one repository a single gate used by local hooks and CI.

## Inputs

Require the repository path, approved checks and write scope. Inspect its agent
rules, existing hooks, gate commands, required tools and Actions workflows.
Preserve existing checks; missing check definitions are "'`CONTRACT_FAILURE`.

## Procedure

1. Inventory each check'"'s command, required tools, area and affected paths.
   Read [the gate contract](references/gate-contract.md) before editing.
2. Reuse an existing compatible "'`tools/ci/gate.sh`; otherwise adapt
   [the template](templates/gate.sh). Its initial hygiene check is only a
   starting point: add every inventoried check, area and path mapping.
   Keep required-tool gaps blocking, and mark the entrypoint executable.
3. Run `bash <skill>/scripts/install-hooks.sh <repo>` to install both hooks
   through `core.hooksPath=.githooks`. Conflicting hooks stop installation;
   integrate their checks into the shared gate before retrying. Never discard
   existing hooks or change global Git settings.
4. Have `setup-a-repo` wire GitHub Actions to the same entrypoint:
   `bash tools/ci/gate.sh <area>` per job. Follow the repository'"'s delivery
   profile; this skill does not choose hosted workflow triggers.
5. In a disposable repository, verify success and introduce a deliberate
   failing change. Confirm both commit and push are blocked with the same
   gate failure, then restore the fixture. Verify "'`--list`, explicit areas,
   `--changed=<base>`, and missing-tool exit 3. Record commands and exit codes.

## Return and recovery

Return `PASS`, `REPAIRABLE_FAILURE`, `CONTRACT_FAILURE`,
`ENVIRONMENT_FAILURE`, or `OWNER_DECISION_REQUIRED` with changed paths,
commands, results and blocker. Missing tools are environmental gaps, never
passes. Retry at most three times, each with new evidence or a new hypothesis;
otherwise stop. Report unrun integration checks. Installation alone is not
proof that the checks pass. Do not merge or publish without task authority.
EOF
cat > skills/setup-pre-commit/references/gate-contract.md <<'"'EOF'
---
type: reference
title: Shared Gate Contract
okf_status: active
tags: [internal, operations]
---
# Shared gate contract

"'`tools/ci/gate.sh [--changed[=<base>]] [--list] [<area>...]`

No areas means all areas. `--list` prints available areas without running
checks. Unknown options, areas or invalid bases exit 2. `--changed` selects
only areas whose paths changed against the base, plus `hygiene`; omitted base
means the merge base of HEAD and origin/main. Include committed, staged,
unstaged and untracked changes, and both sides of renames. Explicit areas
intersect the changed selection; hygiene still runs in changed mode.

Each executed area prints `gate: <area>: PASS|FAIL|GAP <detail>`.
Exit 0 means pass, 1 means a check failed, 2 means invalid usage, and 3 means
a required tool is missing. A gap takes precedence over a check failure.
All selected areas run so one failure does not hide other evidence.

The template implements hygiene with `git diff --check HEAD --` and has no
project-specific checks. Before adoption, extend `areas`, `area_matches`,
and `run_area` with the repository'"'s inventory. Check each required tool
before invoking it; return 3 for missing tools, 1 for failed checks and 0
for success. Do not turn a tool's arbitrary nonzero status into success.
Changes to shared configuration must select every affected area. Hygiene
checks tracked whitespace only; inventory untracked-file checks separately.

The installer takes one optional repository path (default "'`.`), requires an
executable gate, and installs identical pre-commit and pre-push hooks calling
`bash tools/ci/gate.sh --changed` from the repository root. It refuses
conflicting hook files, symlinks and a different configured hooks directory.
If default hooks are active, migrate them before switching hooksPath.
Repeated installation preserves identical hooks and sets repository-local
`core.hooksPath` to `.githooks`. It never writes global configuration.

Actions and harness hooks use this same entrypoint. Actions can run one area
per job; delegate workflow authoring to `setup-a-repo`. The default changed
mode needs origin/main and a usable merge base; provision those refs or pass
an explicit base. A missing base blocks the gate rather than skipping it.
EOF
cat > skills/setup-pre-commit/templates/gate.sh <<'"'EOF'
#"'!/usr/bin/env bash
set -u

# Extend these three definitions together from the repository'"'s check inventory.
areas=(hygiene)
area_matches() {
    case \""'$1" in
        hygiene) return 0 ;;
    esac
    return 1
}
run_area() {
    case "$1" in
        hygiene) git diff --check HEAD -- ;;
        *) return 2 ;;
    esac
}
usage() {
    printf '"'%s\\n' 'usage: gate.sh [--changed[=<base>]] [--list] [<area>...]' >&2
    exit 2
}
changed=0
list=0
base=
selected=()
for arg in \""'$@"; do
    case "$arg" in
        --changed) changed=1 ;;
        --changed=*) changed=1; base=${arg#*=}; [[ -n "$base" ]] || usage ;;
        --list) list=1 ;;
        -*) usage ;;
        *)
            known=0
            for area in "${areas[@]}"; do [[ "$arg" == "$area" ]] && known=1; done
            ((known)) || usage
            selected+=("$arg") ;;
    esac
done
if ((list)); then printf '"'%s\\n' \""'${areas[@]}"; exit 0; fi
for tool in git mktemp; do
    if ! command -v "$tool" >/dev/null; then
        printf '"'gate: hygiene: GAP required tool missing: %s\\n' \""'$tool"
        exit 3
    fi
done
root=$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel) || usage
cd "$root" || exit 1
paths=()
if ((changed)); then
    if [[ -z "$base" ]]; then base=$(git merge-base HEAD origin/main) || usage; fi
    base=$(git rev-parse --verify --end-of-options "$base''^{commit}") || usage
    changes=$(mktemp) || exit 1
    trap '"'rm -f \""'$changes"'"' EXIT
    git diff --no-renames --name-only -z \""'$base" -- > "$changes" || exit 1
    git ls-files --others --exclude-standard -z >> "$changes" || exit 1
    mapfile -d '"'' -t paths < \""'$changes"
fi
((${#selected[@]})) || selected=("${areas[@]}")
status=0
for area in "${areas[@]}"; do
    wanted=0
    for request in "${selected[@]}"; do [[ "$area" == "$request" ]] && wanted=1; done
    if ((changed)) && [[ "$area" == hygiene ]]; then wanted=1; fi
    ((wanted)) || continue
    if ((changed)) && [[ "$area" != hygiene ]]; then
        affected=0
        for path in "${paths[@]}"; do
            if area_matches "$area" "$path"; then affected=1; break; fi
        done
        ((affected)) || continue
    fi
    # A subshell prevents a check'"'s exit from hiding later area results.
    (run_area \""'$area")
    rc=$?
    case "$rc" in
        0) printf '"'gate: %s: PASS checks completed\\n' \""'$area" ;;
        3|127) printf '"'gate: %s: GAP required tool missing\\n' \""'$area"; status=3 ;;
        *) printf '"'gate: %s: FAIL check exit %s\\n' \""'$area" "$rc"
           ((status == 3)) || status=1 ;;
    esac
done
exit "$status"
EOF
cat > skills/setup-pre-commit/scripts/install-hooks.sh <<'"'EOF'
#"'!/usr/bin/env bash
set -euo pipefail
[[ $# -le 1 ]] || { echo '"'usage: install-hooks.sh [repository]' >&2; exit 2; }
root="'$(git -C "${1:-.}" rev-parse --show-toplevel)
cd "$root"
[[ -x tools/ci/gate.sh ]] || { echo '"'missing executable tools/ci/gate.sh' >&2; exit 1; }
configured="'$(git config --get core.hooksPath || true)
[[ -z "$configured" || "$configured" == .githooks ]] || {
    echo '"'conflicting core.hooksPath; integrate existing hooks first' >&2; exit 1;
}
[[ "'! -L .githooks ]] || { echo '"'refusing symlink .githooks' >&2; exit 1; }
if [[ -z \""'$configured" ]]; then
    hooks=$(git rev-parse --git-path hooks)
    for file in "$hooks"/*; do
        [[ "$file" == *.sample || ! -x "$file" || -d "$file" ]] || {
            echo '"'active default hooks; integrate existing hooks first' >&2; exit 1;
        }
    done
fi
hook='#"'!/usr/bin/env bash
set -euo pipefail
cd "$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)"
exec bash tools/ci/gate.sh --changed'"'
for name in pre-commit pre-push; do
    file=.githooks/"'$name
    [[ ! -L "$file" ]] || { echo "refusing symlink $file" >&2; exit 1; }
    if [[ -e "$file" ]] && { [[ ! -f "$file" ]] || [[ $(cat "$file") != "$hook" ]]; }; then
        echo "conflicting $file; integrate existing checks first" >&2
        exit 1
    fi
done
mkdir -p .githooks
for name in pre-commit pre-push; do
    printf '"'%s\\n' \""'$hook" > ".githooks/$name"
    chmod +x ".githooks/$name"
done
git config --local core.hooksPath .githooks
printf '"'%s\\n' 'Installed pre-commit and pre-push: tools/ci/gate.sh --changed'
EOF
