+Give one repository a single gate used by local hooks and CI.
+
+## Inputs
+
+Require the repository path, approved checks and write scope. Inspect its agent
+rules, existing hooks, gate commands, required tools and Actions workflows.
+Preserve existing checks; missing check definitions are `CONTRACT_FAILURE`.
+
+## Procedure
+
+1. Inventory each check's command, required tools, area and affected paths.
+   Read [the gate contract](references/gate-contract.md) before editing.
+2. Reuse an existing compatible `tools/ci/gate.sh`; otherwise adapt
+   [the template](templates/gate.sh). Its initial hygiene check is only a
+   starting point: add every inventoried check, area and path mapping.
+   Keep required-tool gaps blocking, and mark the entrypoint executable.
+3. Run `bash <skill>/scripts/install-hooks.sh <repo>` to install both hooks
+   through `core.hooksPath=.githooks`. Conflicting hooks stop installation;
+   integrate their checks into the shared gate before retrying. Never discard
+   existing hooks or change global Git settings.
+4. Have `setup-a-repo` wire GitHub Actions to the same entrypoint:
+   `bash tools/ci/gate.sh <area>` per job. Follow the repository's delivery
+   profile; this skill does not choose hosted workflow triggers.
+5. In a disposable repository, verify success and introduce a deliberate
+   failing change. Confirm both commit and push are blocked with the same
+   gate failure, then restore the fixture. Verify `--list`, explicit areas,
+   `--changed=<base>`, and missing-tool exit 3. Record commands and exit codes.
+
+## Return and recovery
+
+Return `PASS`, `REPAIRABLE_FAILURE`, `CONTRACT_FAILURE`,
+`ENVIRONMENT_FAILURE`, or `OWNER_DECISION_REQUIRED` with changed paths,
+commands, results and blocker. Missing tools are environmental gaps, never
+passes. Retry at most three times, each with new evidence or a new hypothesis;
+otherwise stop. Report unrun integration checks. Installation alone is not
+proof that the checks pass. Do not merge or publish without task authority.
